[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi! I'm trying to encode parameterized modules in ivy code into Veil2 and I'd like some guidance on the same. I'm working with the following example from IVy repo: <br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kenmcmil/ivy/blob/master/examples/ivy/toy_lock_udp/toy_lock.ivy\">https://github.com/kenmcmil/ivy/blob/master/examples/ivy/toy_lock_udp/toy_lock.ivy</a></p>\n<p>Specifically, the code fragment for the counter and total-order:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">total</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">order</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">helper</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">total_order</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kn\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">                        </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Reflexivity</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kn\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Transitivity</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kn\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Anti</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">symmetry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kn\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">             </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Totality</span>\n<span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">relation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">epoch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">epoch</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">instantiate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">total_order</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">epoch</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">counter</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">incr</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">returns</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">assume</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"n\">xff</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">output</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The Rabia protocol description has some guidance on translating the <code>total_order</code> as a class, based on the <code>ThreeValuedType</code> class: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- axiomatising an enumerate type containing three distinct elements: `v0`, `v1`, and `vquestion`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ThreeValuedType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">vquestion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- axioms</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ax1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ax2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vquestion</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ax3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vquestion</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ax4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vquestion</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- (source: https://github.com/verse-lab/veil/blob/main/Examples/Rabia/Rabia.lean)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, I'm unsure of the encoding for the <code>counter</code> as it has actions defined within it.<br>\nAs far as I know, the examples of protocols implemented in the Veil repo, do not have any examples of parameterized modules. Please let me know how we may encode the same. Thank you for your help.</p>",
        "id": 581416845,
        "sender_full_name": "prash",
        "timestamp": 1774369134
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"543536\">@prash</span> We currently don't have support for parameterised modules, although we've done all the preparatory work to make it possible. It's definitely a priority, but I'm currently writing up my dissertation, so don't have time to dedicate to it. The plan is to start working on it in a few months' time. </p>\n<p>Basically, the advice for now is:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If the module doesn't have actions, use a Lean <code>class</code></li>\n<li>If the module has actions, specialise it for the actual use-site and inline it in the parent module</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In Ivy, the module system is primarily meant as a way to manage undecidability of verification conditions. That is less of a concern in Veil because you'd be able to prove these goals manually / with interactive proofs. (Claude Code is very good at solving goals generated by Veil.)</p>",
        "id": 581512399,
        "sender_full_name": "George Pîrlea",
        "timestamp": 1774405124
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you have a specific use-case that you think really needs modules (and can share about it), I'd be happy to jump on a call and give you more directed advice on what the possible workarounds could be. Please DM me in that case, and we can schedule something.</p>",
        "id": 581512562,
        "sender_full_name": "George Pîrlea",
        "timestamp": 1774405245
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"542918\">@George Pîrlea</span>  for this detailed response. I shall try to work with this information and reach out to you, if I hit a road block. All the best with your dissertation work!</p>",
        "id": 581787841,
        "sender_full_name": "prash",
        "timestamp": 1774488175
    }
]